# The suffix grammar has teeth, ruled in July, again on 2026-09-03, and
# reversed into its present shape on 2026-09-16: a `!` name answers an effect,
# the box a failure bubbles through, the way `foo[k]!` answers a box holding
# the element or the missing-index err. A declaration wearing the bang and
# delivering a plain string tells the reader the opposite of what it does.
#
# This compiled clean before the contract was enforced, and printed `hi!`.
fn shout! x
  "{x}!"

pub play = print (shout! "hi")
